scope: |
  build-rust emits a crate MISSING the defs it could not lower, then lets rustc blame the user's own
  call site. rozum's downstream binary (clients/meeting, :8405) cannot be rebuilt. Three ssc-level
  diagnostics naming the real cause used to print and now do not -- the def is dropped BEFORE
  RustCodeWalk.renderDef, since walk() itself returns Left(diags) correctly. Find the swallow first;
  the List lowering gap (Nil pattern, Cons extractor, `::`) is the second, separate half.
next: FOUND -- build-rust only honours markdown-LINK imports; a bare .ssc keeps the import inside
